[x] 58 CPU building-block nodes -- a minimal kit for wiring an ultra-primitive
       clocked CPU (fetch/decode/execute) on a worksheet. Decode/dispatch reuses
       existing Filters (each node has only one output port); the ALU stays
       PnExpression/PnExpression2. Four new GTK-free core nodes in a "CPU"
       palette group, no ABI bump (leaf nodes only). Key correctness rule: the
       write/load/reset ports are SILENT (latch, emit nothing), so a register or
       counter can sit in a feedback loop without forming a *synchronous* cycle
       -- the value is read back on the next clock tick, keeping each machine
       cycle well under PN_NODE_MAX_DISPATCH_DEPTH (256).
       [x] 58.1 PnRegister (lib/pn-register.c) -- wire-writable value latch
             (accumulator / register / flag store). Inputs 0 write (silent),
             1 read/clock (emits stored value + output/success), 2 reset. The
             "initial" property also seeds the stored latch.
       [x] 58.2 PnCounter (lib/pn-counter.c) -- self-advancing register, the
             program counter. Inputs 0 tick (emit then advance by step, wrap at
             modulo), 1 load (JUMP target, silent), 2 reset. A load landing
             during a tick's synchronous emit overrides that cycle's advance
             (pending-write applied after the emit unwinds), so a decoded JMP
             takes effect on the next tick.
       [x] 58.3 PnRam (lib/pn-ram.c) -- addressable read/write memory, PROM-
             compatible addressing (data.value = address). data.write true
             stores data.word (silent); otherwise reads the word onto
             data.value and echoes data.address. Reuses PROM's image parser for
             the optional "contents" seed.
       [x] 58.4 PnMux (lib/pn-mux.c) -- value-selected multiplexer. Input 0
             select (0-based, clamped) plus 2..8 collated data inputs
             in1..inN; forwards the selected line's value when the selector
             changes or the selected line updates.
       [x] 58.5 Factory registration (pn-node-factory.c), lib + data
             Makefile.am, per-node help pages
             (data/help/Pn{Register,Counter,Ram,Mux}.html).
       [x] 58.6 Unit tests (tests/unit/test-pn-{register,counter,ram,mux}.c):
             latch/read/reset; tick/advance/modulo + JUMP-during-tick; RAM
             write/read/miss/seed; mux routing/clamp/resize.
       [x] 58.7 Runnable example
