[x] 66 Shift Register node -- and the multi-output ports it needs. One input,
       N outputs (2..16, "outputs" property). Every arriving message is stored
       at the head of an open-ended shift register: message k leaves on
       output 1, message k-1 on output 2, ... message k-N+1 on output N; the
       oldest falls off the end. Stages not yet filled stay silent. Emission
       order is oldest stage first, output 1 last, so a downstream multi-input
       node triggered from output 1 already sees the other stages updated.
       This settles the port-model question #56 left open: multi-output is
       the mirror image of multi-input.
       [x] 66.1 Core port model (pn-node): pn_node_set/get_n_outputs,
             per-output names (node-set, default "out1".., not serialized),
             per-output last-value readout, pn_node_emit_message_on_output()
             + pn_node_current_output() (thread-local, saved/restored like
             current_input). pn_node_emit_message() == output 0. The stacked
             port section is max(multi-in rows, multi-out rows). No ABI bump
             (instance-private state + new functions only).
       [x] 66.2 PnWire source_output ("source-output" property,
             pn_wire_new_ports()); a wire forwards only emissions on its own
             output.
       [x] 66.3 Serialization: optional "source_output" on connections (load,
             save, clipboard paste); omitted when 0 so existing files stay
             byte-identical.
       [x] 66.4 Worksheet: output tabs down the right edge of the port
