[x] 70 Tapped Delay node -- one input, N outputs (2..16, "outputs"). Every
       arriving message is forwarded unchanged on each output, output k after
       k * "step-ms" milliseconds (output 1 after one step, output N after N
       steps). A time-staggered fan-out: cascading light chases, staggered
       device start-up, echo effects. Unlike the Shift Register (shifts by
       message count) this shifts by time; unlike Delay, one message yields N
       spaced copies. Core, Filters/Timing.
